{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b5969c65-8070-4e0c-b3cd-97e4036cd634","agentId":"a29267e13ff18cadf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (FastAPI cuore/; mes lib via cuore/services/*_bridge.py; Jinja globals via the side-effect imports liveboard_routes.py uses). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no commits, never open COM3 or call live adapter endpoints (car on the bench, main session owns it); TestClient + fixture observations only. Minimal grepping. Report under 120 words. Another agent is editing cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py, cuore/live/store.py, cuore/live/ops.py, bench/report/job/system templates, tests.html: do NOT edit those; you may read them. You own only NEW files plus one import+include_router pair in cuore/app.py and one line in cuore/web/templates/_vtabs.html (More menu).\n\nOwner's question: \"does CUORE have a log area to save the freeze frame data?\" Today live reads land in CUORE_STATE_DIR/observations.jsonl as from-car observations (kinds obd_dtcs, readiness, mode06, soon freeze_frame; real examples dated 2026-10-13 in C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl -- read a few for shapes, copy into your fixture, never modify that file) and MES logs live in MultiEcuScan's folder. There is no browsable scan log. Build one:\n1. cuore/live/scanlog.py: group from-car observations (live_store.is_from_car) per VIN into \"scans\": consecutive observations within a 15-minute window = one scan {id SCAN_<yymmddHHMM>, vin, started, ended, source (stream text, adapter identity if present), ecus, dtcs {stored, pending, permanent}, readiness, mil, freeze_frames (per DTC/ECU, every PID with name/value/unit), mode06 (per MID/TID value/min/max/pass), pids (latest value per PID in the window), counts}. Derived on read, cached by observations file mtime; no second copy of the truth. Plus export(scan_id, fmt): \"json\" and \"mes\" -- the MES-style text log format the mes library already parses (grep the parser in mes-log-mcp/mes for the scan log format once: list_logs/read_log; produce a file the parser accepts, written under CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/SCAN_<yymmddHHMM>.txt, stamped \"source: cuore live read, serial COM3\"), so existing MES tooling and the workup can read live scans unchanged. Never write into MultiEcuScan's own folder.\n2. cuore/services/scanlog_bridge.py: list_scans(vin), scan(vin, id), diff(vin, id_a, id_b) (codes added/removed, freeze-frame field deltas, Mode 06 pass/fail changes, readiness changes), export.\n3. cuore/api/scanlog.py: GET /api/scans/{vin}, GET /api/scans/{vin}/{id}, GET /api/scans/{vin}/{id}/export?fmt=json|mes, GET /api/scans/{vin}/diff?a=&b=. Read-only.\n4. cuore/web/scanlog_routes.py at /v/{vin}/scans (+ /v/{vin}/scans/{id}): templates/scanlog.html + scan.html, static/scanlog.css: list newest first (date, source, MIL, codes chips, counts), detail page with sections Codes, Readiness, Freeze frames (one table per code: PID, name, value, unit -- all PIDs, sentence case), Mode 06 (MID/TID, name, value, min, max, PASS/FAIL chip), Live PIDs, \"Compare with previous scan\" (diff rendered), Export JSON / Export MES log buttons, print stylesheet with the \"as of\" stamp. Shop-floor rules: 16px, 48px targets, marque theme, nothing under 12px, no horizontal page scroll (tables in overflow-x containers). \"Scans\" entry in the More menu of _vtabs.html.\n5. Tests cuore/tests/check_scanlog.py: fixture observations (today's shapes: 2 obd_dtcs reads + readiness + mode06 + freeze_frame if the kind exists, 3 minutes apart; plus one older group) → 2 scans; the newest has stored P0440, pending P0455, MIL on, Mode 06 3A FAIL; freeze-frame table lists fuel_level; diff reports P0440 added; MES export file parses with the mes parser (import it and read back codes); demo/replay observations are excluded; pages 200; unknown scan 404. Run it plus check_screens.py."},"uuid":"e737389d-768a-4cc7-beb4-77ee41af311a","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:20:53.678Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
