{"parentUuid":"e3c3cb2c-77fa-45ee-95d6-176818feed8c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a29267e13ff18cadf","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1CHfFhNgfiCcNae4v3b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E4SMf1qUosrgmk5L8AbxKQ","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Built the scan log feature end to end. New files only, plus the two permitted edits.\n\nNew: cuore/live/scanlog.py (groups from-car observations into 15-min-window scans, caches on observations.jsonl mtime/size, diff(), export_mes_text()/write_mes_export() under CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/ — never MultiEcuScan's folder); cuore/services/scanlog_bridge.py; cuore/api/scanlog.py (/api/scans/{vin}, /{id}, /diff, /{id}/export?fmt=json|mes); cuore/web/scanlog_routes.py (/v/{vin}/scans, /scans/{id}); templates scanlog.html + scan.html; cuore/web/static/scanlog.css (scoped overrides so this page hits 12px-min/48px-target even where the shared sheet runs smaller); cuore/tests/check_scanlog.py.\n\nEdited (as scoped): cuore/app.py — one import+include_router pair for the api router, one for the web router. cuore/web/templates/_vtabs.html — added \"scans\" to the More-menu tuple and one vtab() line.\n\nKey design notes: obd_dtcs/freeze_frame observations often carry vin=\"\" (Mode 03/06 doesn't ask); a scan's VIN is borrowed from any readiness/mode06/identity row in its own time window. Freeze frames are built from the live \"freeze_frame\" kind — I found mid-task that another agent had just wired _observe for it in ops.py, and its shape matched what I'd already defensively coded. SCAN-format export unions stored/pending/permanent per ECU (real SCAN logs have no such distinction either) and parses back cleanly with mes.scan.parse_scan_text.\n\nVerified: check_scanlog.py (45/45) and check_screens.py (28/28) and check_flow_bar.py (45/45, no regression from the _vtabs.html edit) all pass via .venv/Scripts/python.exe. No COM3/live-adapter access at any point — only TestClient and hand-built fixture observations.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":222889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01E4SMf1qUosrgmk5L8AbxKQ":{"message":"Built the scan log feature end to end. New files only, plus the two permitted edits.\n\nNew: cuore/live/scanlog.py (groups from-car observations into 15-min-window scans, caches on observations.jsonl mtime/size, diff(), export_mes_text()/write_mes_export() under CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/ — never MultiEcuScan's folder); cuore/services/scanlog_bridge.py; cuore/api/scanlog.py (/api/scans/{vin}, /{id}, /diff, /{id}/export?fmt=json|mes); cuore/web/scanlog_routes.py (/v/{vin}/scans, /scans/{id}); templates scanlog.html + scan.html; cuore/web/static/scanlog.css (scoped overrides so this page hits 12px-min/48px-target even where the shared sheet runs smaller); cuore/tests/check_scanlog.py.\n\nEdited (as scoped): cuore/app.py — one import+include_router pair for the api router, one for the web router. cuore/web/templates/_vtabs.html — added \"scans\" to the More-menu tuple and one vtab() line.\n\nKey design notes: obd_dtcs/freeze_frame observations often carry vin=\"\" (Mode 03/06 doesn't ask); a scan's VIN is borrowed from any readiness/mode06/identity row in its own time window. Freeze frames are built from the live \"freeze_frame\" kind — I found mid-task that another agent had just wired _observe for it in ops.py, and its shape matched what I'd already defensively coded. SCAN-format export unions stored/pending/permanent per ECU (real SCAN logs have no such distinction either) and parses back cleanly with mes.scan.parse_scan_text.\n\nVerified: check_scanlog.py (45/45) and check_screens.py (28/28) and check_flow_bar.py (45/45, no regression from the _vtabs.html edit) all pass via .venv/Scripts/python.exe. No COM3/live-adapter access at any point — only TestClient and hand-built fixture observations.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"db2779fc-872e-4778-b547-8bec7263dd1c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg1CHex6FDCpVanoZZop4","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"88675f9a-bc44-44c4-99c0-1c1f77df7c16","timestamp":"2026-10-14T00:38:03.854Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
